<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.3.4: Solving More Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00412</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.3.4: Solving More Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8adb98a6-0104-4325-acc4-1d59c772da57</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Solve this system of equations without graphing. Be prepared to show your reasoning. Use
        this system of equations to answer questions 1 – 3.</para>
      <para id="para-00002"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para><!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
      <!--Q1-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> value?</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00005"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->

        <exercise id="_1d10d402-b443-4531-bfcf-dc65abd33808" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00006">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> value?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Correct! 6</para>
            <para id="para-00008">Nice try! The correct answer is 6.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
      <!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
      <!--Q3-->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">Explain your solutions.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00011">Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>Substituting <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the first equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, gives
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, which then gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.
              Substituting <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the first equation and solving for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>
              gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item>The first equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, can be rearranged to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.
              Substituting <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the second equation gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.
              Solving this equation leads to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, and substituting <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in either equation gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>Building Character: Growth Mindset</title>
          
            <media alt="Illustration of a person in a lab coat on a ladder watering a brain with orange clouds and leaves, symbolizing nurturing growth and creativity; gears in the background suggest ideas or mental processes.">
              <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_05_09_01.png" width="200px"/>
            </media>
          
            <para id="para-00012">Having a growth mindset means believing you can improve your abilities. Compared
        to a fixed mindset, a growth mindset encourages you to embrace challenges, sustain effort,
        and try new strategies. Think about your current sense of having a growth
        mindset. Are the following statements true for you??</para>
            <list id="list-00002">
              <item>After I make a mistake, I always look for ways to learn from it. </item>
              <item>I love challenges because they make me smarter. </item>
            </list>
            <para id="para-00013">Don’t
        worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your
        first step starts today!</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
